"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\lambda \\notdivides x$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L31_lambda_not_dvd_x
msgid "Let $K = \\Q(\\zeta_3)$ be the third cyclotomic field. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}_K = \\Z[\\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}^\\times_K$ be the group of units of $\\cc{O}_K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\zeta_3 \\in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\lambda \\notdivides x$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L31_lambda_not_dvd_x
msgid "By contradiction, if $\\lambda \\divides x$, then\n"
"$\\lambda^{3n-1} \\divides \\lambda^{3n-2}  x = a+b$. Using *lmm:lambda_dvd_a_add_eta_mul_b*\n"
"and *lmm:lambda_dvd_a_add_eta_sq_mul_b*, we have that $\\lambda^{3n+1} \\divides\n"
"(a+b)  (a + \\eta  b)  (a + \\eta^2 cdot b) = a^3+b^3\n"
"= u c^3 = u \\lambda^{3n} w^3$.\n"
"Then $\\lambda \\divides w^3$ which implies that $\\lambda \\divides w$, that\n"
"contradicts *lmm:lambda_not_dvd_w* forcing us to conclude $\\lambda \\notdivides x$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L31_lambda_not_dvd_x
msgid "Level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L32_coprime_x_y
msgid "coprime_x_y"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L32_coprime_x_y
msgid "Let $S$ be a $solution$ with multiplicity $n$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\gcd(x,y) = 1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L32_coprime_x_y
msgid "Let $S$ be a $solution$ with multiplicity $n$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\gcd(x,y) = 1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L32_coprime_x_y
msgid "Since $y \\neq 0$ by *lmm:lambda_not_dvd_y*, by the properties of PIDs it suffices to prove that\n"
"$\\forall p \\in \\cc{O}_K$ if $p$ is prime and $p \\divides x$, then $p \\notdivides y$.\n"
"Let $p \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be prime and suppose by contradiction that $p \\divides x$ and $p \\divides y$\n"
"which implies that $p \\divides \\lambda^{3n-2} x = a+b$ and $p \\divides \\lambda y = a + \\eta b$.\n"
"Then by *lmm:associated_of_dvd_a_add_b_of_dvd_a_add_eta_mul_b*\n"
"we have that $p$ is associated with $\\lambda$, which implies that $\\lambda \\divides x$\n"
"that contradicts *lmm:lambda_not_dvd_x* forcing us to conclude that $p \\notdivides y$, which,\n"
"as stated above, implies that $\\gcd(x,y)=1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L32_coprime_x_y
msgid "Level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

