"Let $\\cc{O}_K = \\Z[\\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}^\\times_K$ be the group of units of $\\cc{O}_K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\zeta_3 \\in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\lambda \\notdivides Z$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L43_lambda_not_dvd_Z
msgid "Let $K = \\Q(\\zeta_3)$ be the third cyclotomic field. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}_K = \\Z[\\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}^\\times_K$ be the group of units of $\\cc{O}_K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\zeta_3 \\in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\lambda \\notdivides Z$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L43_lambda_not_dvd_Z
msgid "By contradiction we assume that $\\lambda \\divides Z$, then, by the properties of divisibility,\n"
"$\\lambda \\divides u_3 Z^3$, which implies, by *$u_1,u_2,u_3,X,Y,Z$*,\n"
"that $\\lambda \\divides z$.\n"
"However, this contradicts *lmm:lambda_not_dvd_z*\n"
"forcing us to conclude that $\\lambda \\notdivides Z$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L43_lambda_not_dvd_Z
msgid "Level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L44_coprime_Y_Z
msgid "coprime_Y_Z"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L44_coprime_Y_Z
msgid "Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\gcd(Y, Z) = 1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L44_coprime_Y_Z
msgid "Let $S$ be a $solution$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $\\gcd(Y, Z) = 1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L44_coprime_Y_Z
msgid "Since $Z \\neq 0$ by *lmm:lambda_not_dvd_Z*, by the properties of PIDs it suffices to prove that\n"
"$\\forall p \\in \\cc{O}_K$ if $p$ is prime and $p \\divides Y$, then $p \\notdivides Z$.\n"
"Let $p \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be prime and suppose by contradiction that $p \\divides Y$ and $p \\divides Z$\n"
"which implies that $p \\divides u_2 Y^3 = y$ and $p \\divides \\lambda u_3 Z^3 = z$.\n"
"But this contradicts *lmm:coprime_y_z* forcing us to conclude that $p \\notdivides Z$, which,\n"
"as stated above, implies that $\\gcd(Y,Z)=1$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L44_coprime_Y_Z
msgid "Level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L45_formula1
msgid "formula1"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L45_formula1
msgid "Let $K = \\Q(\\zeta_3)$ be the third cyclotomic field. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}_K = \\Z[\\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}^\\times_K$ be the group of units of $\\cc{O}_K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\zeta_3 \\in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$ with multiplicity $n$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $u_1 X^3 \\lambda^{3n-2}+u_2 \\eta Y^3 \\lambda +\n"
"u_3 \\eta^2 Z^3 \\lambda = 0$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L45_formula1
msgid "Let $K = \\Q(\\zeta_3)$ be the third cyclotomic field. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}_K = \\Z[\\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\cc{O}^\\times_K$ be the group of units of $\\cc{O}_K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\zeta_3 \\in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\eta \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\\zeta_3 \\in K$. \\\\\n"
"Let $\\lambda \\in \\cc{O}_K$ be such that $\\lambda = \\eta -1$. \\\\\n"
"Let $S$ be a $solution$ with multiplicity $n$.\\\\\\\\\n"
"Then $u_1 X^3 \\lambda^{3n-2}+u_2 \\eta Y^3 \\lambda +\n"
"u_3 \\eta^2 Z^3 \\lambda = 0$."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L45_formula1
msgid "Applying *$u_1,u_2,u_3,X,Y,Z$*,\n"
"*lmm:toInteger_cube_eq_one* and *lmm:toInteger_eval_cyclo*, we have\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"u_1 X^3 \\lambda^{3n-2}+u_2 \\eta Y^3 \\lambda + u_3 \\eta^2 Z^3 \\lambda\n"
"&= x \\lambda^{3n-2} + \\eta y \\lambda + \\eta^2 z \\lambda \\\\\n"
"&= (a+b) + \\eta (a+\\eta b) + \\eta^2 (a+\\eta^2 b) \\\\\n"
"&= a (1 + \\eta + \\eta^2) + b (1 + \\eta^4 + \\eta^2) \\\\\n"
"&= (a+b)(1+\\eta+\\eta^2)\\\\\n"
"&= (a+b)0 = 0\n"
"\\end{align*}"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.FermatSLastTheoremForExponent3.L45_formula1
msgid "Level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

